WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.689
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:02.689 --> 00:00:04.120
Everybody loves.

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:08.450
Every single person at some point has that
small moment of bliss that changes the rest

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:09.750
of their life.

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:14.570
And we’re not the only ones, even animals
have fully monogamous relationships.

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.630
Look they cuddle and everything.

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:18.310
But what exactly is love?

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:22.269
Let’s finally answer the question that’s
perplexed scientists for generations.

00:00:22.269 --> 00:00:34.730
Oh and if you stay long enough I might even
tell you how you can make someone love you.

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:37.930
Love is free, it can’t be owned, bought
or sold.

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:41.680
Is has no mass or weight and cannot be touched.

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:45.910
Yet it is the single most powerful emotion
humans can experience.

00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:48.559
It makes us do some really stupid stuff sometimes.

00:00:48.559 --> 00:00:53.539
But it’s far more than an emotion, it can
physically affect our bodies in some rather

00:00:53.539 --> 00:00:55.570
incredible ways.

00:00:55.570 --> 00:01:00.840
For example, some extraordinary research revealed
that when two lovers gaze into each others

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:06.170
eyes, their heart rates synchronise and beat
at the exact same time.

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:10.570
This graph shows the heart rates of two individuals
in love, whilst their eyes were locked in

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.229
a loving exchange.

00:01:12.229 --> 00:01:17.200
The red line shows one heart beat, the blue
line the other, notice how their heart rates

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:22.549
are so closely matched, so much so, that the
blue line can barely be seen beneath the red

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:24.090
line.

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:27.270
Love is also a powerful pain killer.

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:33.240
In fact, cuddling can cure a headache, during
a loving embrace the chemical Oxytocin is

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:36.880
released in our brains, ovaries and testicles.

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:41.630
Research has found that a dose of Oxytocin
can significantly decrease headaches and other

00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:42.630
pains.

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:46.820
Studies have also shown that simply looking
at a photo of a loved one can reduce pain

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:49.110
by up to 40%.

00:01:49.110 --> 00:01:51.909
So then, what is love?

00:01:51.909 --> 00:01:58.909
Well, this really depends on how you look
at it, some people say love is down to fate,

00:01:58.909 --> 00:02:02.119
our path is already decided, out of our control.

00:02:02.119 --> 00:02:08.500
That sure sounds poetic, but the processes
associated with love can actually be extrapolated

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:12.000
and explained to a large extent by science.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:18.000
But I should warn you, this won’t be romantic,
unless statistics turn you on.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:23.700
Psychologists have shown that it takes anywhere
between 90 seconds and 4 minutes to decide

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:25.380
if you fancy someone.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:30.701
Surprisingly being attracted to someone has
very little to do with what they say, research

00:02:30.701 --> 00:02:37.700
shows that 55% is through body language, 38%
is the tone and speed of their voice and only

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:40.620
7% is down to what they say.

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:47.060
In order to properly explain love we must
first break it down into its 3 stages, lust,

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:48.540
attraction and attachment.

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:53.270
Each stage is driven by its own set of unique
hormones and chemicals.

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:58.710
A person must go through all 3 stages before
they can truly be in love with someone, which

00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:02.310
kind of puts a spanner in the whole “love
at first sight” thing.

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:07.570
The first stage, Lust is probably the most
biologically simple, lust is driven by the

00:03:07.570 --> 00:03:10.870
sex hormones testosterone and oestrogen.

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:15.630
In fact research shows that women actually
have different tastes in men whilst using

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:17.510
contraception.

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:24.100
Women taking the pill prefer men with more
feminine faces, whereas women not using contraception

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:26.200
prefer more masculine men.

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:31.170
But what’s even more interesting is that
the features that trigger lust in a person

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:33.360
differs between genders.

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:38.561
Research shows that men are attracted to women
that have a symmetrical face, full lips, full

00:03:38.561 --> 00:03:44.940
breasts, and wide hips compared to their waist
size, or to put in more simply an hourglass

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:45.940
figure.

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:50.430
Because statistically curvy women are also
the most fertile.

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:55.760
In fact there’s actually some maths behind
this, in European countries the most desirable

00:03:55.760 --> 00:04:03.340
waist-to-hip ratio in women is 0.7, and in
South America and Africa it’s 0.9.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:07.450
On the other hand, women prefer men with broad
shoulders and a narrow waist.

00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:14.260
But most intriguingly, one of the most desirable
qualities in a man is a healthy immune system.

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:18.851
Research shows that women are subconsciously
attracted to men with healthy faces, because

00:04:18.851 --> 00:04:21.720
this signals a strong immune system.

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:26.620
Stage 2 is Attraction, this is the stage when
you’re deeply in love and you can’t think

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:29.610
of anything but your new partner.

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:35.030
Scientists think there are three main neurotransmitters
involved with this stage, adrenaline, dopamine

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:36.450
and serotonin.

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:41.470
Firstly, adrenaline along with the stress
hormone cortisol are released in your body

00:04:41.470 --> 00:04:44.760
during the first few weeks of your new relationship.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:49.410
These two chemicals are responsible for making
you sweat, increasing your heart rate and

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:53.460
giving you a dry mouth when you’re around
your new love interest.

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:58.600
Secondly, your levels of dopamine increase,
this gives you an intense rush of pleasure

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:04.350
when you bump into your new love and it’s
what makes you desire them even more.

00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:08.700
Increased dopamine levels also increase your
energy levels, and decrease your need for

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:09.970
sleep and food.

00:05:09.970 --> 00:05:13.990
It actually has a very similar effect on the
brain as taking cocaine.

00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:20.220
And finally, whilst you’re in the attraction
stage, your levels of the serotonin neurotransmitter

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:22.100
drop dramatically.

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:26.620
This causes you to become obsessed with your
new love interest, it’s the reason they

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:30.030
keep popping into your thoughts throughout
the day.

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:34.990
Interestingly the low serotonin levels experienced
by new lovers are remarkably similar to the

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:39.810
low serotonin levels found in patients with
Obsessive-Compulsive Disorder.

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:45.370
Lastly, the final and most important stage
of love is attachment.

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:49.940
During this stage the powerful bond is formed
that keeps some couples together for life

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:52.950
and makes them want to have children.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:58.100
Research shows there are two major hormones
responsible for this feeling of attachment.

00:05:58.100 --> 00:05:59.780
Oxytocin and vasopressin.

00:05:59.780 --> 00:06:06.360
Both the oxytocin and vasopressin hormones
are released by men and women, when they kiss,

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:08.840
cuddle and have sex.

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:14.070
Scientists believe that the more sex a couple
has, the deeper their bond becomes.

00:06:14.070 --> 00:06:17.770
An interesting example of this can be seen
with prairie voles.

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:23.980
Like humans, they indulge in far more sex
than is necessary for the purpose of reproduction,

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:29.450
and they also, like humans, form stable pair-bonds.

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:34.430
As part of an experiment, scientists gave
prairie voles a drug that suppresses the effect

00:06:34.430 --> 00:06:36.600
of the vasopressin hormone.

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:41.830
Something remarkable happened, their bond
with their partner deteriorated immediately

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:45.960
and they no longer protected their partner
from potential new suitors.

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:51.710
So in a nutshell, the answer to the question
“What is love?”, is “Love is a state

00:06:51.710 --> 00:06:57.430
of deep attachment to a fellow human being,
caused by a combination of chemicals.

00:06:57.430 --> 00:07:05.770
Specifically: Testosterone, Oestrogen, Adrenaline,
Dopamine, Serotonin, Oxytocin and Vasopressin”.

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:07.690
Sounds so romantic doesn’t it?

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:11.960
I do apologise if I’ve somewhat ruined the
magic.

00:07:11.960 --> 00:07:16.560
But remember, these are nothing more than
scientific explanations for a set of symptoms

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:19.790
and behaviours associated with being in love.

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:25.550
In reality, love truly is a seemingly magical
and rather beautiful, force of nature that

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:28.639
could never be fully explained by science.

00:07:28.639 --> 00:07:35.380
But there’s still the question of “why”
does love exist, what purpose does it serve?

00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:39.160
Evolutionary scientists believe that love
is a product of evolution.

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:41.140
The theory goes like this.

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:46.500
Without love acting as the glue, in a relationship,
keeping a partner long enough to reproduce

00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:47.500
is difficult.

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:52.880
If love wasn’t a component in most relationships,
they most likely wouldn’t last longer than

00:07:52.880 --> 00:07:54.170
a couple of weeks.

00:07:54.170 --> 00:07:57.440
Which, means a lot fewer couples would reproduce.

00:07:57.440 --> 00:08:03.200
It’s love, that keeps relationships together
for several years or more, long enough for

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:09.040
them to have children, which, after all is
the ultimate goal of evolution.

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:14.000
Scientists believe that over millions of years,
humans, and certain other animals, have developed

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:19.090
a specific set of chemical processes, to make
us feel like we are emotionally attached to

00:08:19.090 --> 00:08:21.180
our potential mating partner.

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:26.180
Thus giving us an incentive to want to stay
together and ultimately reproduce.

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:31.350
We, however, interpret this, as being in love.

00:08:31.350 --> 00:08:37.190
But you may be thinking, if the sole purpose
of love is just an incentive to reproduce.

00:08:37.190 --> 00:08:39.580
Then why do we love our family, and even our
pets?

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:44.650
It all has to do with the attachment hormone
we talked about before, Oxytocin.

00:08:44.650 --> 00:08:50.330
It isn’t just released when we have sex,
it’s also released in somewhat smaller doses

00:08:50.330 --> 00:08:53.730
when we simply touch another person, or animal.

00:08:53.730 --> 00:08:59.050
Every time we touch another person and experience
a release of Oxytocin, we become more deeply

00:08:59.050 --> 00:09:00.500
attached to them.

00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:05.940
And who do you think you came in contact with
the most as a baby, that’s right, your family.

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:09.740
Ever heard the phrase “There’s nothing
like a mother’s love”.

00:09:09.740 --> 00:09:14.550
Well there really isn’t, during the later
stages of pregnancy Oxytocin levels in the

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:20.850
mother surge to unfathomably high levels,
these levels peak right at the moment of childbirth.

00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:25.860
This creates a seemingly unbreakable bond
and an unrivalled level of attachment between

00:09:25.860 --> 00:09:27.589
the mother and child.

00:09:27.589 --> 00:09:31.440
But it’s not just humans that release Oxytocin.

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:38.120
Scientists have discovered that dogs and cats,
among many other animals, also release Oxytocin

00:09:38.120 --> 00:09:42.200
when they come into physical contact with
another animal, or human.

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:48.880
So good news animal lovers, this means, that
your pet really does love you too.

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:52.910
Scientists found that the more you socially
interact with your pet, the more deeply they

00:09:52.910 --> 00:09:58.110
become attached to you, and hence the more
deeply they will fall in love with you.

00:09:58.110 --> 00:10:03.300
So then, like I promised here’s how you
can make someone fall in love with you.

00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:08.399
It’s really quite simple, find a potential
new suitor, it doesn’t even have to be someone

00:10:08.399 --> 00:10:09.790
you know.

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:14.930
Reveal some intimate details about your life
to them, then stare deeply into their eyes

00:10:14.930 --> 00:10:16.390
for 4 minutes.

00:10:16.390 --> 00:10:21.640
There’s a slight chance you may get a slap,
but research shows that more often than not

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:24.480
they will feel strangely attracted to you.

00:10:24.480 --> 00:10:29.740
New York psychologist, Professor Arthur Arun,
demonstrated this when he randomly paired

00:10:29.740 --> 00:10:35.090
people together from a group of complete strangers
and asked them to reveal intimate details

00:10:35.090 --> 00:10:40.350
about their lives to each other for 30 minutes,
then stare deeply into each other’s eyes

00:10:40.350 --> 00:10:42.240
for 4 minutes.

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:47.100
Afterwards nearly all of the couples admitted
to feeling deeply attracted to the stranger,

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:50.649
whom they had only spent 34 minutes with.

00:10:50.649 --> 00:10:55.279
And following the experiment one of the couples
actually got married.

00:10:55.279 --> 00:10:59.779
If for some weird reason you don’t feel
comfortable imposing your newly learned Jedi

00:10:59.779 --> 00:11:01.470
mind tricks on a complete stranger.

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:07.470
Fear not, there are some slightly less insane
things you can do to increase the chances

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:10.080
of your crush falling in love with you.

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:13.350
Research shows that proximity has a huge effect
on love.

00:11:13.350 --> 00:11:19.050
A study in Ohio showed that 54% of couples
who recently applied for marriage licenses

00:11:19.050 --> 00:11:25.940
were separated by a distance of 16 blocks
or fewer and 37% were less than 5 blocks apart

00:11:25.940 --> 00:11:27.240
from each other.

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:30.130
The science behind this is repeated exposure.

00:11:30.130 --> 00:11:34.290
The more you see someone or something the
more you like it.

00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:40.320
However this is not always the case, repeated
exposure to another person amplifies the dominant

00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:42.740
emotion in the relationship.

00:11:42.740 --> 00:11:48.100
So if the dominant emotion is anger or hate,
they’re just going to dislike you even more.

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:52.350
But the bottom-line is, if you want someone
to fall in love with you, you should spend

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:55.690
as much time as possible in their company.

00:11:55.690 --> 00:11:58.089
Unless you really, really annoy them.

00:11:58.089 --> 00:12:02.610
Research shows that individuals whom are in
a state of emotional distress are significantly

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:04.250
more likely to fall in love.

00:12:04.250 --> 00:12:08.800
This state of emotional unease is often found
following the death of a loved one, being

00:12:08.800 --> 00:12:13.320
in an accident, or most commonly, after a
painful breakup.

00:12:13.320 --> 00:12:18.290
Obstacles that stand in the way of love can
actually increase the chance of a relationship

00:12:18.290 --> 00:12:19.290
forming.

00:12:19.290 --> 00:12:24.240
Studies show that attraction is actually increased
when external factors get in the way.

00:12:24.240 --> 00:12:30.089
A great example of this is when teenagers
start a relationship and their parents object,

00:12:30.089 --> 00:12:33.700
it only makes the teenagers want to be together
even more.

00:12:33.700 --> 00:12:37.230
Finally, I’ll leave you with these facts.

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:42.240
Women tend to find men twice as attractive
when they notice other women are interested

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:43.240
in him.

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:48.640
Also, on average, a man will spend one year
of his life staring at women.

00:12:48.640 --> 00:12:53.080
It’s also common to think that men are less
emotionally affected by relationships than

00:12:53.080 --> 00:12:54.080
women.

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:59.540
But statistically, men are quicker than women
to say “I love you” in relationships and

00:12:59.540 --> 00:13:06.480
contrary to popular belief, recent studies
have shown that men are more emotionally affected

00:13:06.480 --> 00:13:11.360
when a relationship ends than women.

